<title>USA: Thermadyne completes Italian acquisition.</title>
<headline>Thermadyne completes Italian acquisition.</headline>
<dateline>ST. LOUIS 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thermadyne Holdings Corp on Monday said it completed the acquisition of  GenSet S.p.A., an Italian manufacturer of engine-driven welders and auxiliary power generators for about $28 million.</p>
<p>GenSet, whose main operations are in Pavia, Italy, generated sales of about $38 million and earnings before tax, depreciation, amortization and other non-cash charges (EBITDA) of $4.8 million for the year ended December 31.</p>
<p>Thermadyne is a multinational manufacturer of cutting, welding, wear-resistant and hard-facing products.</p>
<p>	     ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
